    "configuration": {
      "title": "Snd",
      "properties": {
        "snd.path": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "snd",
          "markdownDescription": "The Snd executable. Left at `snd`, the extension prefers a binary bundled under `bin/<platform>-<arch>/` (see `tools/build-snd.sh`) and falls back to `PATH`. Set an absolute path to override both — that wins over everything. Whether a build has a GUI is decided when it is compiled (`--with-motif`); this setting picks a binary, it cannot switch a GUI on."
        },
        "snd.mode": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "auto",
            "nogui",
            "gui"
          ],
          "default": "auto",
          "markdownDescription": "Which binary to guess when `snd.path` is left at `snd`: `nogui` tries `snd-nogui`, `gui` tries `snd-motif`. Both modes are driven the same way; in `gui` mode Snd's own window comes up as well and stays usable."
        },
        "snd.args": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "default": [],
          "markdownDescription": "Extra arguments for Snd. The bridge is appended with `-l` afterwards. `~/.snd` is deliberately NOT suppressed — add `-noinit` here if you want a bare session."
        },
        "snd.startOnActivation": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "description": "Start a Snd session as soon as a Scheme file is opened. Off by default: Snd claims the audio device on startup."
        },
        "snd.keymap": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "inf-snd",
            "slime",
            "none"
          ],
          "default": "inf-snd",
          "markdownEnumDescriptions": [
            "`inf-snd.el`, Snd's own Emacs mode: `C-c C-e` definition, `C-c C-r` region, `C-c C-o` file, `C-c C-l` load, `C-c C-i` help, `C-c C-p` play, `C-c C-t` stop, `C-c C-z` REPL, `C-c C-f` open sound.",
            "SLIME/SLY: `C-x C-e` last expression, `C-M-x` definition, `C-c C-r` region, `C-c C-p` eval and print, `C-c C-k` load, `M-.` source, `C-c C-d C-d` describe, `C-c C-d C-a` apropos.",
            "No keybindings; everything stays reachable from the command palette."
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "Which keymap to use. The default is `inf-snd.el`'s, because it is Snd's own: these chords are what a Snd user's hands already do, and `C-c C-p` for *play* and `C-c C-t` for *stop* only exist in a keymap written for a sound editor. The setting is exclusive rather than additive, because three chords disagree between the two: `C-c C-p` is eval-and-print in SLIME, `C-c C-t` is trace, and `C-c C-e` is an eval prompt. Two meanings on one chord is worse than either choice."
        },
        "snd.openReplOnStart": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Open the REPL terminal whenever a session starts. On by default: a running Snd with no visible listener is a process nobody can type into, and Snd's own stdout — its warnings and anything it prints on its own account — has nowhere to appear. The focus is not taken, so starting a session by evaluating a form leaves the cursor in the file."
        },
        "snd.sourcePath": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "",
          "markdownDescription": "Where the Snd sources are, so that `(load-from-path \"v.scm\")` finds Snd's own Scheme files — `v.scm` (the fm-violin), `clm-ins.scm`, `dsp.scm`, `examp.scm`, `ws.scm`. These ship with Snd; the sound files everybody quotes (`oboe.snd`, `fm-violin.snd`) do **not**, and are downloaded separately. Empty means: use the source tree `tools/build-snd.sh` left in `.build`, if there is one, and otherwise leave `*load-path*` alone."
        }
      }
    },
    "languages": [
